From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:01:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] J714s: 15 s Stage 1 proxy window; switchable uncompressed
 Mach-O enrollment

omarchy-j714s 1 powers off about 4 s after the progress bar once the
padded Aura Mach-O Stage 1 is enrolled with kmutil configure-boot
--compress (docs/install-failure-2026-11-13.md). Nothing appeared on the
USB cable because the engine filled window_ms 0, and --compress is one of
four things that changed since the 2026-11-07 trial that booted.

- omarchy_asahi.py: BOARD_MACHO["j714sap"] window_ms 0 -> 15000, so Aura
  opens its USB proxy for 15 s before it chainloads Stage 2 and a boot
  that stops early is visible on the cable. BoardMachO gains a compress
  field (default True; j714sap names True), passed to Recovery staging.
- omarchy_recovery.py: stage() takes macho_compress (a bool, default True)
  and writes it into the Mach-O mode of the startup bundle's manifest:
  modes.macho = {espPath, executeWindow, compress}.
- Recovery app: AuraBootMode.machoCompression(entry) reads "compress"
  (missing key = true, so older bundles stay compressed; anything but a
  JSON boolean is refused); enrollmentArguments(..., compress:) passes
  --compress only when true; stageExpandedStage1 checks that kmutil
  offers --compress only when compressing. Padding, kmutil inspect,
  bputil and the rest of the Mach-O path are unchanged. BootSelectionCheck
  covers both argument forms and the manifest key.
- Default unchanged: the J714s still enrolls compressed. Uncompressed
  needs compress=False on the board row and a new engine.
- Engine renamed v0.9.2-omarchy.20261113.9360b4de398f and repacked from
  the authenticated engine.28 base: 17912715 bytes, sha256
  5caff1afed8833d809fd61a5de48d766c2e6592640b0125abe2a49e601a333a2, two
  identical repacks.

Checked on Linux: engine overlay tests (432), engine tooling tests,
test/all, image-builder/test/all (except the edge-dispatch template test
that already fails on release 1), engine_pin.py check,
verify-source-lock.py, read-validation-engine.py, prepare-engine.py.
BootSelection.swift + BootSelectionCheck.swift compiled and passed with
Swift 6.2 on Linux (a test-only CFGetTypeID shim; Linux Foundation lacks
it), and swift-format 6.2.4 lint --strict passes on the changed Swift.

Not yet checked: the Recovery app build and its fixtures need a macOS run
(installer-app.yml or the Recovery fixture workflow). After that run,
build-input-provenance.json's recovery block (run, artifact, zip sha256,
inventory sha256, tree, commit; set by patches-j714s 0007) must be
updated to it: the Recovery tree changes with this patch.

Uncompressed enrollment keeps the 300 s authorization limit
(Recovery/Native/Authorization.c grants 3600 s only to configure-boot
--compress).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
